  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency WASH and Protection support to conflict-displaced communities in Hiraan and Galmudug Regions, Central South Somalia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main aim of this $1,685,000 UNICEF project is to provide life-saving WASH and comprehensive child protection services. To that end, UNICEF will provide safe drinking water through trucking and water point repairs, construct communal latrines, distribute hygiene kits and raise awareness around good hygiene practices. UNICEF will also provide protection support for unaccompanied and separated children and psychosocial counselling for children and caregivers. In total, UNICEF will reach 60,000 people through the WASH component, including 12,600 women and 18,600 girls, and 20,000 people through the child protection component, including 3,000 women and 7,500 girls.</narrative>
  </description>
